1
00:04:32,727 --> 00:04:38,727
Hear how it all began.

2
00:09:05,454 --> 00:09:11,454
A Quiet Place: Day One is a horror, science fiction,
thriller film directed by Michael Sarnoski.

3
00:13:38,181 --> 00:13:44,181
As New York City is invaded by alien creatures who hunt by sound,
a woman named Sam fights to survive with her cat.

4
00:18:10,909 --> 00:18:16,909
Samira, played by Lupita Nyong'o.

5
00:22:43,636 --> 00:22:49,636
Eric, played by Joseph Quinn.

6
00:27:16,363 --> 00:27:22,363
Reuben, played by Alex Wolff.

7
00:31:49,090 --> 00:31:55,090
Henri, played by Djimon Hounsou.

8
00:36:21,818 --> 00:36:27,818
Zena, played by Eliane Umuhire.

9
00:40:54,545 --> 00:41:00,545
Osahar, played by Takunda Khumalo.

10
00:45:27,272 --> 00:45:33,272
A Quiet Place: Day One is a 2024 American apocalyptic horror film, written and directed
by Michael Sarnoski, based on a story he conceived with John Krasinski.

11
00:50:00,000 --> 00:50:06,000
It is the third installment in the A Quiet Place film
series, and a prequel to the first two films.

12
00:54:32,727 --> 00:54:38,727
The film stars Lupita Nyong'o as a terminally ill woman during the early stages of an invasion in
New York City by blind extraterrestrial creatures with an acute sense of hearing.

13
00:59:05,454 --> 00:59:11,454
The supporting cast includes Joseph Quinn and Djimon Hounsou,
who reprises his role from A Quiet Place Part II.

14
01:03:38,181 --> 01:03:44,181
Development on A Quiet Place: Day One began in November 2020,
with Jeff Nichols set to write and direct.

15
01:08:10,909 --> 01:08:16,909
Despite a completed script, Nichols dropped out of the film in October 2021.

16
01:12:43,636 --> 01:12:49,636
In January 2022, Sarnoski was announced to replace Nichols as writer and director; he was
approached by Krasinski because of his feature directorial debut Pig (2021).

17
01:17:16,363 --> 01:17:22,363
Principal photography took place from February 2023
to April 2023 in London, England.

18
01:21:49,090 --> 01:21:55,090
A Quiet Place: Day One premiered at the Tribeca Festival on June 26, 2024, and was
released in the United States by Paramount Pictures on June 28.

19
01:26:21,818 --> 01:26:27,818
The film received generally positive reviews from critics and grossed
$262 million worldwide on a $67 million production budget.

20
01:30:54,545 --> 01:31:00,545
The film explores themes of monster, escape, cat, alien, prequel.

21
01:35:27,272 --> 01:35:33,272
The tone is uplifting and dark and thought_provoking.
